# Every text file is LF in every checkout (owner 2026-11-15: tests failed on the
# owner's Windows PC and passed in CI). Git for Windows checks text out as CRLF by
# default, and many tests here read source files and match them line by line
# (lobby: forgetPresentationKey, overlayFit, settingsCopy, WeatherScene; site: the
# page tests), so a Windows checkout failed them with nothing wrong. The repo has
# always stored LF; this only stops Windows turning it into CRLF on the way out.
# shared/.gitattributes says the same for the brand kit, which is copied byte for byte.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are run by cmd.exe, which wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# A saved copy of the church's calendar page, kept exactly as it was fetched.
lobby/src/lib/__fixtures__/calendar-2026.html -text
